Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 11:04:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 68/69] freedreno/a2xx: round bilinear weights on Xenos

Xenos truncates bilinear weights to 1/64 (measured: floor(frac * 64) / 64,
no coordinate offset), up to 4/255 too dark for 8-bit colors. Fragment
shaders add half a step, 1/128 texel of the base level from a per-sampler
constant (212 + sampler, zero for nearest filtering and for the gmem
programs), to 1D/2D/3D/rect coordinates so the truncation rounds.
piglit 1-1-linear-texture and fbo-blit-stretch pass.

